.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-payload-field 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-payload\-field \- Print one field of a hook payload read from stdin, for a shell hook that must not depend on jq
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten payload field\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-harness\fR> <\fB\-\-name\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print one field of a hook payload read from stdin, for a shell hook that must not depend on jq
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-harness\fR
The harness whose payload dialect to decode
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
claude\-code: Claude Code\*(Aqs `PreToolUse` payload; a deny is returned as the `hookSpecificOutput.permissionDecision` JSON object on stdout with exit `0` — the channel the production shell guards already use
.IP \(bu 2
cursor: Cursor. Two payload families under one host: a generic `preToolUse` that looks like Claude\*(Aqs, and specialized events (`beforeShellExecution`, `beforeReadFile`, `beforeMCPExecution`) that carry the operand at top level and **no** `tool_name` at all. Session is `conversation_id`
.IP \(bu 2
copilot\-cli: GitHub Copilot CLI, registered in its **`PascalCase`** dialect — which yields `hook_event_name` natively. The camelCase dialect omits the event name entirely, so Batten does not speak it
.IP \(bu 2
gemini\-cli: Gemini CLI. Claude\-identical payload fields, different event names (`BeforeTool` rather than `PreToolUse`)
.IP \(bu 2
codex\-cli: Codex CLI, whose wire format is a near\-verbatim clone of Claude Code\*(Aqs — its own repo says so. No payload shim is needed; the adapter exists so the host is nameable and its fixture is pinned against drift
.IP \(bu 2
exit\-code: The neutral core contract: envelope in, decision as exit code out — `0` allow, `2` deny (reason on stderr), for any host whose only decision channel is an exit status. Both codes are the §7 table\*(Aqs, unmodified
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR
Which payload field to print; an allowlist, never a JSON path
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
hook\-event\-name: The host\*(Aqs own event spelling, echoed back untouched
.IP \(bu 2
session\-id: The host\*(Aqs session id
.IP \(bu 2
tool\-name: The tool being mediated
.IP \(bu 2
command: The command text, for shell\-shaped tools
.IP \(bu 2
cwd: The host\*(Aqs working directory
.IP \(bu 2
stop\-hook\-active: Whether this is a re\-entered `Stop` hook
.IP \(bu 2
last\-assistant\-message: The assistant\*(Aqs last message
.IP \(bu 2
transcript\-path: The path to the session transcript
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
